{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall discern from all the people.</b> You must select and appoint them yourself, for in these three matters it is required that you yourself be involved, and no one else will suffice. But in the matter of rendering particular judgments, the officers of thousands, officers of hundreds, etc. will suffice. For indeed, when there are four ranks, one above the other, the lesser judge first, and the one who cries out against his verdict may cry out to the one above him — from the second to the third, and from the third to the fourth — and so those who come before you for judgment will be few."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:09.758798523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}